+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+A merge inserted two new functions between an existing rustdoc block and the function the
+block documents. Rustdoc now attaches those blocks to the wrong items:
+
+- In `apps/cli/src/commands/execution/mod.rs`, `repository_scope` was inserted between
+  `addressable_scope`'s doc block ("The ONE scope the `execution` verbs can address for a
+  given execution id.", including its `# Errors` section) and `addressable_scope` itself. The
+  error contract is documented on a function that takes no arguments and cannot fail.
+- In `apps/cli/src/commands/mcp/tools.rs`, `assign_schema` was inserted between
+  `synthesize_schema`'s doc block ("Closed like every other schema here. `fixture` and
+  `route` are both optional…") and `synthesize_schema` itself. The doc names fields
+  (`fixture`, `route`) that exist only in the `synthesize` schema.
+
+Anyone reading the crate's rustdoc — operator-facing tool tables, `cargo doc` output, IDE
+hovers — sees another function's documentation. The blocks describe the displaced functions'
+signatures and failure modes, not the items they now sit on.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Move `addressable_scope`'s displaced doc block (the "The ONE scope …" paragraph group,
+  including its `# Errors` section) back directly above
+  `pub(crate) fn addressable_scope` in
+  `apps/cli/src/commands/execution/mod.rs`. `repository_scope` keeps the three-line block that
+  already describes it ("The same addressing rule as [`addressable_scope`]…").
+- Move `synthesize_schema`'s displaced doc block (the "Closed like every other schema here…"
+  paragraph) back directly above `fn synthesize_schema` in
+  `apps/cli/src/commands/mcp/tools.rs`. `assign_schema` keeps no doc block of its own (it has
+  none to restore).
+- Comments only: no code tokens, no signatures, no reformatting, no other files changed. No
+  runtime, wire, CLI-output, or dependency impact.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `cli-rustdoc`: the CLI crate's rustdoc attributes every doc block to the item it documents —
+  in particular the execution scope-addressing helpers (`addressable_scope`,
+  `repository_scope`) and the MCP tool-schema builders (`synthesize_schema`, `assign_schema`).
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+(none — the repository has no existing specs; this is a new capability for a repo whose
+`openspec/specs/` was just initialized.)
+
+## Impact
+
+- Files touched: exactly two, both inside `apps/cli/src/commands/` —
+  `execution/mod.rs` and `mcp/tools.rs`. Each diff moves a contiguous block of `///` lines
+  within the same file; every line is removed once and re-added once, unchanged.
+- Observability: the observable contract is rustdoc attachment. It can be observed from this
+  checkout by (a) checking the source adjacency of each doc block and its function, and (b)
+  building `cargo doc -p graphhelm-cli --no-deps --document-private-items` and asserting each
+  generated HTML page documents the intended text for the intended function. A workspace-wide
+  build or full test suite is not required; a comments-only move cannot change codegen.
+- Risk: minimal. The only hazard is an edit that touches more than the two comment blocks
+  (verified by a clean, block-only diff and `cargo fmt --check` staying green).
